            <div xml:id="d411">

                <pb facs="0769" n="645" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg645"/>

                <head>No. 407.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Mr. Langston</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-07-06"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 6,
                        1881</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 156.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your No. 389 of the 18th
                    ultimo, touching the probable repeal of the law fixing a tax of one per cent.
                    for consular visas. The information contained in Mr. Laforestrie’s private note
                    to you of the 15th June is acceptable, and I trust that the wise resolution of
                    the Haytian Government to procure the abolition of this obnoxious tax will be
                    speedily accomplished.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JAMES G. BLAINE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
